        text: "The spine runs view, reason, example, contrast. The view states the position plainly: 'cities should pedestrianise their centres'. The reason makes it true: 'because the space a moving car occupies would hold six café chairs or one hundred pedestrians'. The example shows the reason working somewhere real: 'take the case of the street behind our station — two years after the barriers went up, the shops that fought the scheme hardest are the ones expanding now'. The contrast proves you saw the other side: 'admittedly, deliveries get harder, which is why the successful schemes give the first hour of every morning to vans'. Four beats, each one handing the next its subject. Learn the beats, and length stops being a problem — a Part 3 answer can simply be the spine plus one or two extra examples on the same rails.",
